From: Michael Narine <michael@verita-ai.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:48:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Thread: make name_tbb_thread_pool_threads_set_locale() a no-op

name_tbb_thread_pool_threads_set_locale() (called by the first Print::process and SLAPrint::process of the process)
runs a parallel_for of max_concurrency() tasks that all wait for each other, to name the TBB workers and set the C locale
on them. TBB's concurrency is a maximum, not a guarantee: the workers are a shared pool and may be absent or busy in
another arena, so a barrier that needs every thread at once can wait forever. An embedder that runs jobs in its own
arenas (Slicewright) sets the locale on the threads of those arenas with a task_scheduler_observer, and has no use for the
thread names, so the function does nothing in this build.

Purpose: Remove an all-threads-at-once barrier that can hang the first slice of a process; the embedder sets the worker locale itself.
SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
Upstream-Status: Not-upstreamable Orca's GUI relies on it to set the locale of its workers
Orca-Base: v2.4.2
---
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/Thread.cpp b/src/libslic3r/Thread.cpp
--- a/src/libslic3r/Thread.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/Thread.cpp
@@ -211,6 +211,11 @@
 // Also it sets locale of the worker threads to "C" for the G-code generator to produce "." as a decimal separator.
 void name_tbb_thread_pool_threads_set_locale()
 {
+	// Slicewright: a no-op. The barrier below needs all max_concurrency() threads to run a task at the same time, but TBB
+	// only promises a maximum (the workers are a shared pool and may be busy in another arena), so it can wait forever.
+	// The embedder sets the C locale on the threads of its own arenas instead (a task_scheduler_observer).
+	return;
+
 	static bool initialized = false;
 	if (initialized)
 		return;
